---
title: Gaspery Limited
dek: The company the apps ship under. One person, in London.
---

Gaspery Limited is the company behind the software on this site. It was incorporated in England and Wales in August 2026, it is based in London, and it has one employee, which is me.

It exists for an unglamorous reason. The apps had reached the point where they needed somewhere to be sold from, supported, and held accountable, and that place should not be a personal name on an invoice.

## What it ships

[GRØD](/apps/grod) is a private, Mac-native memory for your meetings. It records locally, keeps a note you would actually want to keep, and remembers people rather than speaker labels. It is live.

[tavle.](/apps/tavle) edits the HTML decks Claude generates, visually, without opening an HTML editor. It is in development.

[Afterframe](/apps/afterframe) pulls stills and GIFs straight off whatever is playing on a Plex server. It is in development.

There is a fourth thing in planning. Details when it is ready.

All of them are Mac and iOS software, built in SwiftUI, and they share a bias: local by default, quiet where it can be, no accounts to create if the work does not need one.

## Getting in touch

Support questions, press, and anything contractual go to [alex@gaspery.com](mailto:alex@gaspery.com), which reaches me directly.

The [writing](/writing) elsewhere on this site is mine rather than the company's. It is a notebook, not a blog with a marketing calendar behind it.
